{
  "total": 467,
  "totalPage": 10,
  "page": 9,
  "pageSize": 50,
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a768",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3018,
      "bookHadithIndex": 401,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn Abbas that Usmah bin Zaid said:\"The Messneger of Allah departed from Arafat and I was riding behind him. He started trying to rein in his camel until its ears nearly touched the front of the saddle, and he was saying: 'O people, you must be tranquil and dignified, for righteousness does not come by making camels hurry",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3018-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3018-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3018-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a769",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3019,
      "bookHadithIndex": 402,
      "text": "It was narrated from Abu Ghaftan bin Tarif that he heard Ibn Abbas say:\"When the Messenger of Allah departed he reined in his she-camel until its head touched the middle of his saddle, and he was saying to the people: 'Be tranquil be tranquil,' on the evening of Arafat",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3019-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3019-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3019-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a76a",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3020,
      "bookHadithIndex": 403,
      "text": "It was narrated from Al-Fadl bin Abbas, who rode behind the Messenger of Allah, that:on the eveing of Arafat and on the morning of Jam (Al-Muzdalifah), when they departed, the Messenger of Allah said to the people: \"You must be tranquil,\" and was reining in his she-came. Then, when he was in Muhassir, which is part of Mina, he said: \"You have to look for pebbles the size of date stones of fingertips,\" with which to stone the Jamrat. And the Messenger of Allah continued to recite the Talbiyah until he stoned Jamrat Al-Aqabah",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3020-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3020-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3020-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a76b",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3021,
      "bookHadithIndex": 404,
      "text": "It was narrated that Jabir said:\"The Messenger of Allah departed (From Arafat) in a tranquil manner, and he enjoined them to be tranquil. He hurried in the valley of Muhassir and told them to stone the Jamrat with (pebbles like date stones or fingertips. (Daif)",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3021-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3021-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3021-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a76c",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3022,
      "bookHadithIndex": 405,
      "text": "It was narrated from Jabir that the Prophet departed from Arafat and started saying:\"Be tranquil, O slaves of Allah!\" gesturing with his hand like this - and Ayyub gested with his palm uppermost",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3022-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih Lighairihi"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3022-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3022-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a76d",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3023,
      "bookHadithIndex": 406,
      "text": "It was narrated from Usmah bin Zaid that he was asked how the Prophet traveled during the Farewell pilgrimage. He said:\"He used to ride at a moderately fast pace, and when he came upon some open space he would gallop",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3023-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3023-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3023-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a76e",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3024,
      "bookHadithIndex": 407,
      "text": "It was narrated from Usmah bin Zaid that when the Prophet departed from Arafat he turned toward the mountain pass. I said to him:\"Are you going to pray Magrib?\" He said: \"The prayer place is still ahead of you",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3024-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3024-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3024-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a76f",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3025,
      "bookHadithIndex": 408,
      "text": "It was narrated that Usmah bin Zaid said:\"The Messenger of allah stopped in the mountain pass where the rulers stop now, and urinated, then he performed a light Wudu and I said: 'O Messenger of Allah (isit time for ) prayer?' He said: 'The prayer is still ahead of you.' When we came to Al-Muzdalifah the people did not unload their camles until he had prayed",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3025-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3025-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3025-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a770",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3026,
      "bookHadithIndex": 409,
      "text": "It was narrated from Abu Ayyub that:the Messenger of Allah joined Maghrib and Isha in Jam (Al-Muzdalifah)",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3026-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3026-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3026-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a771",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3027,
      "bookHadithIndex": 410,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn Masud that:the Prophet joined Maghrib and Isha in Jam (Al-Muzdalifah)",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3027-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3027-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3027-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a772",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3028,
      "bookHadithIndex": 411,
      "text": "It was narrated from Salim, from his father, that:the Messenger of Allah joined Maghrib and Isha; in Jam (Al-Muzdalifah), with one Iqamah, and he did not offer any voluntary prayers in between or after either of them",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3028-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3028-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3028-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a773",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3029,
      "bookHadithIndex": 412,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn Shihab that Ubaidullah bin Abdullah told him that his father said:\"The Messenger of Allah joined Maghrib and Isha with no (Voluntary) prayer in between them. He prayed Maghrib with three Rakahs and Isha with two.\" And Abdullah bin Umar used to join them in like manner until he met Allahm, The Mighty and Sublime",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3029-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3029-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3029-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a774",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3030,
      "bookHadithIndex": 413,
      "text": "It was narrated that Ibn Umar said:\"The Messenger of Allah prayed Maghrib and Isha in Jam (Al-Muzdalifah) with one Iqamah",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3030-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3030-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3030-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a775",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3031,
      "bookHadithIndex": 414,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibrahim bin Uqbah that Kuraib said:\"I asked usamah bin Zaid, who rode behind the Messenger of Allah one the evening of Arafat. I said: \"What did you do?' He said: 'We started traveling until we reached Al-Muzadalifah, then he stopped and prayed Maghrib. Then he sent word to the people to stay in their camps, and they did not unload their camels until the Messenger of Allah had prayed the later Isah. Then the people unloaded their camels and made camp. When morning came I set out on foot amonth those of the Quraish who got there first, and Al-Fadl rode behind the Prophet",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3031-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3031-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3031-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a776",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3032,
      "bookHadithIndex": 415,
      "text": "It was narrated that Ubaidullah bin Abu Yazeed said:I heard Ibn Abbas say: I was one of those whom the Prophet sent ahead amongh the weak ones of his family",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3032-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3032-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3032-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a777",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3033,
      "bookHadithIndex": 416,
      "text": "It was narrated Abbas said:\"I was one those whom the Prophet sent ahead on the night of Al-Muzdalifah among the weak ones of his family",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3033-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3033-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3033-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a778",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3034,
      "bookHadithIndex": 417,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn Abbas, from Al-Fadl, that:the Prophet commanded the weak ones among Banu Hashim to move on from Jam' (Al-Muzadalifah) at night",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3034-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3034-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3034-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a779",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3035,
      "bookHadithIndex": 418,
      "text": "It was narrated from Salim bin Shawwal that:Umm Habibah told him that the Prophet told her to leave Jam (Al-Muzdalifah) for Mina at the end of the night",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3035-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3035-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3035-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a77a",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3036,
      "bookHadithIndex": 419,
      "text": "It was narrated that Umm Habibah said:\"We used to leave Jam Al-Muzdalifah for Mina at the end of the night, during the time of the Messenger of Allah",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3036-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3036-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3036-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a77b",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3037,
      "bookHadithIndex": 420,
      "text": "It was narrated that Aishah said:\"The Prophet allowed Sawdah to leave Jam (Al-Muzdalifah) before dawn because she was a heavyset woman",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3037-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3037-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3037-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a77c",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3038,
      "bookHadithIndex": 421,
      "text": "It was narrated that Abdullah said:\"I never saw the Messenger of Allah offer any prayer except at the proper time, apart from Maghrib and Isha in Jam (Al-Muzdalifah) and Fajir on that day, which he offered before the usual time",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3038-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3038-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3038-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a77d",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3039,
      "bookHadithIndex": 422,
      "text": "It was narrated that Urwah bin Mudarris said:\"I saw the Messenger of Allah stading in Al-Muzdalifah and he said: 'Whoever offers this prayer whith us here then stands with us and stood before that in Arafat by nightor by day, his Hajj is complete",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3039-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3039-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3039-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a77e",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3040,
      "bookHadithIndex": 423,
      "text": "It was narrated that Urwah bin Mudarris said:The Messenger of allah said: \"Whoever catches up (with Fajir prayer) in Jam (Al-Muzdalifah) with the Imam and the people (and stays there) until they move on, the he has caught up with Hajj. Whoever does not catuch up with the people and the Imam, then has not caught it (Hajj)",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3040-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3040-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3040-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a77f",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3041,
      "bookHadithIndex": 424,
      "text": "It was narrated that Urwah bin Mudarris said:\"I came to the Prohet in Jam (Al-Muzdalifah) and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I have come from the two mountains of Tai and I did not leave any mountain but I stood on it; is there Hajj for me?' The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever offers this prayer with us, and stood before that in Arafatat by night or by day, his Hajj is complete, and he has completed the prescribed duties",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3041-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3041-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3041-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a780",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3042,
      "bookHadithIndex": 425,
      "text": "Urwah bin Mudarris bin Aws bin Harithah bin La'm said:\"I came to the Prophet in Jam (Al-Muzdalifah) and said: 'Is there Hajj for me?' He said: 'Whoever offers this prayer with us and observed this standing until he departed, and he departed before that from Arafat by night or by day, then his Hajj is complete. And he has completed the prescribed duties",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3042-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3042-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3042-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a781",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3043,
      "bookHadithIndex": 426,
      "text": "Urwah bin Mudarris at Tai said:\"I came to the Messenger of Allah and said: \"I have come to you from the two mountains of Tai and I have exhausted my camel, and exhausted myself; is there Hajj for me?' He said: 'Whoever offeres this morning prayer with us here, and came to Arafat before that, then he has completed the prescribed duties and his Hajj is complete",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3043-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3043-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3043-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a782",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3044,
      "bookHadithIndex": 427,
      "text": "Abdur Rahman bin Yamur Ad-Daili said:\"I saw the prophet in Arafat when some people from Najd coame to him. They told a man to ask him about Hajj. He said: \"Hajj is Arafat. Whoever comes on the night of Jam (Al-Muzdalifah) before Subh prayer, then he has caought up with Hajj. And the days of Mina are three days. But whoever hastens to leave in two days, there is no sion on him, and whoever stays on, there is no sino on him.' Then he made a man ride behind him, and he started proclaiming it to the people",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3044-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3044-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3044-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a783",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3045,
      "bookHadithIndex": 428,
      "text": "Jafar bin Muahammad narrated that his father said:\"We came to Jabir bin Abdullah and he told us that the Messenger of Allah said: 'All of Al Muzdalifah is a place for (the pilgrims) to stand",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3045-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3045-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3045-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a784",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3046,
      "bookHadithIndex": 429,
      "text": "It was narrated that Abdur-Rahman bin Yazid said:\"When we were in Jam (Al-Muzadalifah), Ibn Masud said: 'I heard the one to whoem surat Al-Baqarah was revealed say, in this place: Labbaik Allahumma Labbaik",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3046-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3046-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3046-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a785",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3047,
      "bookHadithIndex": 430,
      "text": "It was narrated that Amr bin Maimun aid:\"I head him say 'I saw 'Umar in Al-Muzdalifah and he said: The people of the Jahiliyyah would not depart until the sun had risen, and they would say: Shine, O Thabir! The Messenger of Allah differed from them and departed before the sun had risen",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3047-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3047-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3047-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Bukhari"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a786",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3048,
      "bookHadithIndex": 431,
      "text": "Ata bin Abi Rabah told them that he heard Ibn Abbas say:\"The Messenger of Allah sent me with the weak ones of his family to pray Subh in Mina and stone the Jamrah",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3048-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3048-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3048-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a787",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3049,
      "bookHadithIndex": 432,
      "text": "It was narrated that the Mother of the Belivers Aishah said:\"I wished that I had asked the Messenger of Allah for permission as Sawdha did, so that I could pray Fajir in Mina before the people came. Sawdah was heavyset woman, so she asked the Messenger of Allah for permission, and he gave her permission to pray Fajir in Mina and stone the before the people came",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3049-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3049-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3049-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a788",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3050,
      "bookHadithIndex": 433,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ata bin Abi Rabah that a freed slave of Asma bin Abi Bakr told him:\"I came with Asma bint Abi Bakr to Mina at the end of the night and I said to her: 'We have come to Mina at the end of the night.' She said: 'We sued to do this one who was better than you",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3050-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3050-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3050-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a789",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3051,
      "bookHadithIndex": 434,
      "text": "It was narrated form Hisham bin Urwah that his father said:\"Usamah bin Zaid was asked - while I was sitting with him: 'How did the Messenger of Allah travel during the Farewell Pilgrimage when he moved on?' He said: 'He rode at a moderate pace, and if he found some open space, he would gallop",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3051-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3051-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3051-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a78a",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3052,
      "bookHadithIndex": 435,
      "text": "It was narrated that Al-Fadl bin Abbas said:\"The Messenger of Allah said to the people when they moved on the evening of Arafat and the morning of Jam' (assembly at Al-Muzdalifah): 'You must have tranquility.' He was reining in his camel, and when he entered Mina, he came down to Muhassir and said: 'You have to pick up pebbles the size of date stones of fingertips with which to stone the Jamrat.' And he (Al-Fadl) said: 'And the Prophet gestured with his hand like a man throwing a pebble",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3052-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3052-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a78b",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3053,
      "bookHadithIndex": 436,
      "text": "It was narrated from Jabir that:the Prophet hurried in the valley of Muhassir",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3053-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih Lighairihi"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3053-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3053-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a78c",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3054,
      "bookHadithIndex": 437,
      "text": "Jafar bin Muhamad narrated that hi father said:\"We enterd upon Jabir bin Abdullah and I said: \"Tell me about the Hajj of the Prophet.' He said: 'The Messenger of Allah moved on from Al-Muzadalifah before the sun rose, and Al-Fadl bin Abbas rode behind him. When he came to Muhassir he sped up a little, then he follwed the middle road that brings you out at the largest Jamrat. When he came to the Jamrat whichis by the tree, he threw seven pebbles, saying the Takbir with each one, (using) pebbles the size of the date stones of fingertips, and he threw from the bottom of the valley",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3054-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3054-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3054-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a78d",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3055,
      "bookHadithIndex": 438,
      "text": "It was narrated from Al-Fadl bin abbas that:he was riding behind the Prophet and he continued to recite the Talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrat",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3055-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3055-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3055-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a78e",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3056,
      "bookHadithIndex": 439,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn Abbas that:the Messenger of Allah recited the Talbiyah unitl he stoned the Jamrat",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3056-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3056-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3056-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a78f",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3057,
      "bookHadithIndex": 440,
      "text": "It was narrated that Abu Al-Aliyah said:\"Ibn Abbas said: \"On the morning of Al-Aqabah, while he was on his mount, the Messenger of Allah said to me: \"Pick up (some pebbles) for me.\" So I picked up some pebbles for him that were the size of date stones or fingertips, and when I placed them in his hand he said: \"Like these. And beware of going to extremes in religious matters, for those who came before you were destroyed because of going to extremes in religious matters",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3057-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3057-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3057-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a790",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3058,
      "bookHadithIndex": 441,
      "text": "It was narrated that Al-Fadl bin Abbas said:\"The Messenger of Allah said to the people when they moved on the evening of Arafat and the morning of Jam' (assembly at Al-Muzdalifah): 'You must have tranquility.' He was reining in his camel, and when he entered Mina, he came down to Muhassir and said: 'You have to pick up pebbles the size of date stones of fingertips with which to stone the Jamrat.' And he (Al-Fadl) said: 'And the Prophet gestured with his hand like a man throwing a pebble",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3058-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3058-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3058-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a791",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3059,
      "bookHadithIndex": 442,
      "text": "It was narrated that Ibn Abbas said:\"On the morning of Al-Aqabah, while he was on his mount, the Messenger of Allh said: 'Pick up (some pebbles) for me.' So P picked up some pebbles for him that were the size of date stones of fingertips, and placed them in his hand. He started to do this with his hand.\" Yahya described him shaking them in his hand like this",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3059-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3059-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3059-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a792",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3060,
      "bookHadithIndex": 443,
      "text": "It was narrated from Yajya bin Al-Husain that his grandmother, Umm Husain said:\"I perfomed Hajj during the Hajj of the Prophet. I saw Bilal hodling on the reins of his she-camel, and Usmah bin Zaid hodling his garment ouver him to shade him from the heat, while he was in Ihram, until he had stoned Jamratual Aqabah. Then he addressed the people and praised Allahy, and mentioned many things",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3060-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3060-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3060-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a793",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3061,
      "bookHadithIndex": 444,
      "text": "It was narrated that Qudamah bin Abdullah said:\"I saw the Messenger of Allah stoning JamratualAqabah on the Day of Sacrifice on the reddish-brown camel of his, without beating anyone or driving them off",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3061-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3061-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3061-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a794",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3062,
      "bookHadithIndex": 445,
      "text": "Abu Az-Zubair narrated that he heard Jabir bin Abdullah say:\"I saw the Messneger of Allah stone the Jamrat while on his camel saying: \"O people, learn your rituals (of Hajj) for I do not know whether I will perform Hajj again after this year",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3062-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3062-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3062-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a795",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3063,
      "bookHadithIndex": 446,
      "text": "It was narrated that Jabir said:\"The Messenger of Allah stoned the Jamrat on the Day of Sacrifice in the forenoon, and after the Day of Sacrifice he stoned (the Jamarat) When the sun had passed its zenith",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3063-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3063-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3063-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a796",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3064,
      "bookHadithIndex": 447,
      "text": "It was narrated that Ibn Abbas said:\"The Messenger ofAllah sent us young boys of Banu Abdul-Muttalib on donkeys, stalping our things and saying \"O my sons, do not stone Jamratulal Aqabah until the sun has risen. (Daif)",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3064-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3064-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3064-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a797",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3065,
      "bookHadithIndex": 448,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn Abbas that:the Prophet sent his family ahead, and told them not to stone the Jamrah until the sun had risen. (Daif)",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3065-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3065-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3065-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a798",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3066,
      "bookHadithIndex": 449,
      "text": "Aishah bint Tallah narrated from her maternal aunt Aishah the Mother of the Believers that:the Messenger of Allah told one of his wives to depart from Jam (Al-Muzadalifah) on the night of Jam, to go to Jamratual Aqabah and stone it, then come back to her camp before morning. And Ata used to do that until he died",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3066-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Daif Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3066-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3066-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a799",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 3067,
      "bookHadithIndex": 450,
      "text": "It was narrated that Ibn abbas said:\"The Mesenger of Allah was asked questions during the days of Mina and he said: 'There is no harm.' A man said: 'I shaved my head before offering the sacrifice.' He said: 'There is no harm.' Another man said: 'I stoned (the Majarat) after evening came.' He said: \"There is no harm",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3067-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3067-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-3067-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Bukhari"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}